- EncodeBench execution identity v3 now binds the effective Claude, Codex, and
  OpenAI timeout policies, the per-case generation/retry wall budget, and
  generation retry limits. That budget charges each attempt's source, workspace,
  and prompt setup and bounds backend waits, OpenAI requests and backoffs,
  responses that arrive after the deadline, artifact materialization,
  empty-artifact retries, and all suite retries. Artifacts whose materialization
  crosses the deadline are securely discarded from both the result tree and any
  direct-write backend workspace, then persist as terminal case-budget timeouts.
  Each runner-case receives an independent fresh budget, so runner order and
  runner-set membership cannot consume another runner's allowance or suppress its
  retries. Deterministic artifact validation and optional reviewers pause rather
  than consume the generation budget, so they cannot suppress a permitted
  generation retry and are not misrepresented as preemptible work.
  Capability boards require the complete v3 identity, validate every nested
  checkout and nonempty directory RuleSpec-root field, verify the complete sealed
  PolicyEngine runtime-v2 identity and wrapper digest (including its canonical
  repository and trusted import-path topology), require that runtime whenever
  result rows carry PolicyEngine oracle evidence, and refuse missing or unexpected
  toolchain fields. Admission also mirrors the producer's official/checkout tree
  count equality, canonical RuleSpec runtime-pin path bound to an exact exposed
  RuleSpec execution root (with lexical traversal refused), pin bytes included in
  that checkout's scoped identity and cross-checked by digest, and
  Python-version/stdlib binding. Cross-host PolicyEngine paths normalize to stable
  semantic anchors while import order, relative module origins, and sealed-root
  layout remain score-affecting. Git checkout identities must carry exactly the
  producer-owned scope for the encoder and each RuleSpec root, while the rules
  engine must remain whole-checkout scoped; real producer-to-board admission locks
  protect both contracts. Checkout origins are either absent or use the producer's
  canonical `github.com/<owner>/<repo>` spelling. RuleSpec execution roots must be
  direct jurisdiction children of a matching `rulespec-<country>` checkout with
  that jurisdiction as the first scoped path, and each durable row must use the
  root matching its citation jurisdiction. PolicyEngine rows additionally bind
  the runtime country, exact RuleSpec checkout pin path, and pin digest to that
  same admitted root. Every durable row's admission context must bind back to
  the suite's exact run, manifest, case, corpus, RuleSpec root, runner set,
  execution identity, and digest, and PolicyEngine metrics must bind to that same
  sealed runtime with a required pass outcome and runtime evidence (the score
  remains optional) rather than a producer-impossible partial combination.
  Case identities now expose and bind each case's oracle declaration. Capability
  boards reject successful PolicyEngine cases that omit oracle evidence while
  allowing failed pre-artifact cases to remain outside artifact and oracle
  denominators.
  CLI report admission now delegates execution and row checks to the same strict
  v3 consumer used by capability boards, including scalar and metric types,
  artifact bindings, canonical RuleSpec topology, per-row root jurisdiction,
  PolicyEngine runtime, and timeout/retry policy validation.
  That shared row admission also binds each result's top-level citation to the
  canonical corpus citation in its authenticated case identity.
  Terminal encoder timeout evidence stops suite-level retries, bounding Claude
  and Codex timeout paths to the two documented artifact-generation attempts
  instead of six.
  Runtime retry loops now consume the same bound constants, and completed
  historical runs recover their digest-verified suite retry count before
  rebuilding the live identity, so nondefault policies remain verifiable without
  trusting other persisted execution fields.
- Exhausted encoder timeouts now persist as typed terminal outcomes in eval result
  rows and render as distinct timeout cells on capability boards without entering
  artifact compile, CI, grounding, or reviewer denominators. Durable rows retain
  the exact triggering Codex wall/idle or OpenAI connect/read timeout class and
  threshold even when a longer case deadline also clamps the request, count every
  exhausted OpenAI request attempt (including an alarm wrapped by the HTTP
  stack), retain that history across eventual HTTP responses, and preserve
  earlier generation-time timeout evidence when an artifact is revalidated.
  Codex process completion observed at or after the configured wall deadline is
  now rejected using a monotonic clock instead of being admitted as an on-time
  artifact. Returned or directly written target artifacts from every timed-out
  backend attempt are securely discarded before validation; when the final
  attempt times out, timeout classification takes precedence over any apparent
  artifact validation failure. Capability boards reject contradictory
  terminal-timeout rows that claim a generated artifact. Eval results and
  summaries now use schema v6 with explicit artifact and timeout counts, while
  machine-readable capability boards use schema `axiom-encode/eval-board/v2` for
  the expanded outcome contract.
  Board artifact denominators now require producer-shaped, content-bound output,
  trace, and context-manifest path/digest pairs. Successful PolicyEngine rows
  must carry a passing oracle outcome, passing outcomes may omit an advisory
  score, and artifact-bearing failures cannot evade oracle denominators by
  dropping their metrics. Board admission also requires the producer's core
  artifact digest fields and validates optional validator-verdict path/digest
  pairs without treating verdict-only failure evidence as a generated artifact;
  the producer applies the same PolicyEngine outcome invariants before persistence.
- Reject `.test.yaml` `period_kind` values the Axiom rules engine does not accept during local `validate`. `_coerce_rulespec_period` silently rewrote `period_kind: year` to `tax_year` before its own enum check, so `axiom-encode validate` executed and passed fixtures that the org validate-rulespec workflow's engine test runner then rejected with `unknown variant `year``. Local period coercion now fails closed on any kind outside the engine's serde enum (`month|benefit_week|tax_year|custom`) with a message that names the accepted set and points `year` at `tax_year`, so local validate and the shared workflow agree on which fixtures are executable (axiom-encode#1112, rulespec-dk#2).
- Prevent cited-import prompt guidance from treating displaced `in lieu of` deduction references as mandatory final-amount imports.
- GPT-5.6 OpenAI-backend generations now mark the exact reusable RuleSpec prompt prefix with an explicit cache breakpoint and route it with a model- and schema-bound `prompt_cache_key`; older OpenAI models retain their string input while sharing the same retry-stable key identity. To make that prefix reusable, retry-only validation feedback moves from its former mid-prompt position to immediately before the rejected candidate near the tail; no source, instruction, feedback, candidate, or output-contract text is removed or rewritten. Ordered content blocks preserve the newly assembled prompt byte-for-byte, and the existing compile, CI, grounding, and validation gates remain unchanged. GPT-5.6 requests explicitly use Standard processing, and per-attempt logs now report both `cache_read=` and `cache_write=` so measured savings include cache-write charges; per-attempt, aggregate retry, persisted-session, synchronized-session, and CLI estimates preserve unknown cost outside the configured short-context pricing tier (axiom-encode#1491).
- Add `oracle-coverage --fail-on-empty` so a coverage gate that classifies zero executable outputs fails loudly instead of passing vacuously. `is_composition_policy_repo_root` accepts a directory by name (`rulespec-<country>`) when no `.git` boundary sits at or above it, so a mis-pointed `--root` — a name-shaped non-checkout, an empty `.axiom/` directory or file, an empty pending ledger, an empty jurisdiction directory, or a spurious nested `.git` — builds a zero-output report that satisfies every `--fail-on-*` threshold and the gate goes green (axiom-encode#1113, rulespec-dk#2). `--fail-on-empty` turns a report with no executable outputs at `--root` into a non-zero exit. The decision keys off executable outputs only: program surfaces are the fixed global PolicyEngine variable manifest (independent of `--root`), so `--include-program-surfaces` must not make an empty root look non-empty. It is opt-in because a brand-new jurisdiction repo (e.g. rulespec-tz before its first module merges) is legitimately empty and its push-to-main gate must still pass, so only callers that know outputs are expected set the flag. A non-Git, ProgramSpec-only tree is accepted and classified normally — its `outputs:` yield executable outputs — not rejected as a non-checkout.
- Waiver fingerprints are partition-invariant again: the batch fingerprint executor no longer holds a shared resolution/identity cache across modules (which leaked per-module resolution state between batch neighbors and made failure messages — and therefore fingerprints — depend on chunk layout; observed on rulespec-us as 5/3,099 fingerprints changing between partitions). Only the partition-invariant routing cache spans the batch; each module's validate opens a fresh resolution scope, so every fingerprint equals the module's standalone value under any batch composition or worker fan-out (~8% slower than the shared-cache batch).
- Resolve checkout-root RuleSpec source outputs against the checkout so ProgramSpec signing writes `.axiom/encoding-manifests/programs/...` manifests with `programs/...` citations. (`axiom-encode#1312`)
- Enforce proof-atom anchor consistency in `validate_rulespec_proofs`: a `versions[i].values` atom now requires the version to declare a `values` table and a `versions[i].formula` atom requires the version to declare a `formula`. This makes `versions[i].values` the single authoritative contract for parameter-table proof atoms — the same shape the money-atom gate accepts — resolving the mutual exclusivity where a table atom that satisfied one gate failed the other (axiom-encode#1032, rulespec-be#31/#80).
- `scripts/provision_verification_supervisor.py` now provisions a trusted runtime whose launcher interpreter loads nothing from the user-writable source prefix. The load-bearing guarantee is empirical: the provisioned interpreter is run under a minimal environment and, from a non-empty `/proc/self/maps`, is required to map its own binary from the runtime (non-vacuity, for both shared and static-libpython builds), to map NO file under the source prefix, and to map any `libpython` only from inside the root-owned runtime — holding even under a hostile `LD_LIBRARY_PATH`. (The root-owned system loader and libc legitimately map from `/lib`/`/usr/lib`; the probe bounds the launcher's own load-time closure. C-extensions the encoder imports later are outside this probe: the run-path repin neutralizes their escaping `DT_RPATH`/`DT_RUNPATH`, but an absolute `DT_NEEDED`/`DT_AUDIT` in one is not covered here and remains within the pinned-dependency provenance boundary noted below.) The check observes exactly what the loader does, with no dependence on hand-parsed ELF metadata. Supporting static passes make that outcome reachable and durable: refuse system-python and oversized/symlink-escaping prefixes before copying (the first hosted-runner dispatch copytreed `/usr` because `sudo` secure_path resolved the system interpreter); purge every importable/path-configuration startup carrier after the staged site-packages swap — `.pth`/`._pth`/`sitecustomize`/`usercustomize` in all module forms, `pybuilddir.txt`, and the canonical stdlib `pythonXY[t].zip` across `PLATLIBDIR` variants; and repin every ELF whose `DT_RPATH`/`DT_RUNPATH` (via `patchelf --print-rpath`) escapes the runtime after per-object `$ORIGIN` expansion (both lexical and symlink-resolved containment) to a forced `DT_RPATH` at `<runtime>/lib` that `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` cannot outrank, re-reading to confirm. A new `provision-selftest` workflow exercises the production shape (sudo + resolved toolcache interpreter + `--require-prefix-under` + real patchelf), the self-containment probe, and the fail-closed refusal paths on the hosted Ubuntu image (3.13 + 3.14). Hostile ELF metadata in a pinned dependency is not statically audited — such a dependency already executes its own code inside the signer, so the trust boundary is dependency provenance plus the caller's root-ownership of the finished tree, which the supervisor re-verifies.
- Persisted-row revalidation at eval-suite finalize, resume, and archive now skips advisory reviewers and compares only deterministic validator outputs, so suites with live generalist reviewers can finalize instead of failing on nondeterministic review scores.
- Use one release-aware, fail-closed corpus resolver for generation, validation,
  proof checking, source staleness, and oracle corpus inspection. Applied model
  encodings now pin the resolved source body and carry a signed source
  attestation with release, artifact, row, hash, and date provenance.
- Add strict, expiring validation-failure waivers with protected-base approval,
  deterministic full-failure fingerprints, and independent companion execution.
- Persisted-row revalidation now normalizes outer and inner harness temporary
  paths, subprocess capture paths, and path-bearing capture errors, and
  deterministically orders validation issues, including compile-timeout commands
  and executable-test timeouts.
  Staging roots normalize at quotes, commas, parentheses, and other punctuation
  boundaries without rewriting longer ASCII, composed Unicode, or decomposed
  Unicode path-prefix tokens, so repeated validation of one artifact produces
  identical metrics.
- Classify section 3121 wage-exclusion intermediates in PolicyEngine oracle coverage.
- Classify 3121(y) transferred-federal-employee international-organization employment intermediates as not comparable to PolicyEngine.
- Classify 26 USC 36B(c)(1)(A) applicable-taxpayer helper outputs as not comparable to PolicyEngine final ACA PTC eligibility.
- Classify ACA 36B and 36B(b) PolicyEngine oracle coverage mappings for RuleSpec CI.
- Add a scoped repair for generated ACA section 36B(b) premium-assistance outputs.
- Ground word-form half percentage rates ("five and half per centum", "eighteen and a half per centum") in source-text numeric extraction; bare "half"/"a half" are accepted only next to an explicit percentage marker. Unblocks the Ghana Act 766 SSNIT contribution rates (5.5/13.5/18.5%).
- Allow requested-source RuleSpec validation for 26 USC 3241(b) table headers that name downstream payroll sections as labels, not source citations.
- Fix local corpus lookup for jurisdiction-prefixed source identifiers such as `us-ca:regulation/...`.
- Classify federal CHIP 42 USC 1397jj definition helper outputs as not comparable to PolicyEngine final CHIP child eligibility.
- Tighten encoder guidance and validation for 26 USC 1402(a)(12) so generated self-employment net-earnings deductions stay person-scoped instead of composing stale TaxUnit parent context.
- Project EITC ECPS oracle inputs into Section 1402(b) after generated SECA rules stopped accepting stale Section 1401 self-employment income inputs.
- Admit exact historical generated-v1 HMAC ownership manifests as untrusted
  legacy replacement evidence when the authorized Git base, citation, output
  digest, backend/runner identity, and uniformly scoped applied files all match.
  Manual and generated v1 subclasses remain fail-closed and fresh replacements
  still require current signed v5 provenance.
- Refuse to rewrite a generated RuleSpec artifact that is a symlink, a hard link, or resolves outside the generation's output root, prove that before the unescape pass writes anything, and land the rewrite as a new directory entry rather than in place. Read every fraction-slash run as written (the corpus keeps a mixed number's whole number separated from its fraction; the encoder no longer guesses that markup was flattened). Read Hebrew teen numerals joined by a hyphen or a maqaf, and carry every Hebrew number word into the source-recall inventory as well as the grounding set.
- A fraction-slash run is one value for source recall (an encoding that states 0.25 for `1⁄4` has recalled it; the printed numerator and denominator stay available to grounding but are no longer two further values it owes), keeps a unary minus, and is read only at whole-token boundaries (`1.5⁄2` and `1,000⁄3` are not fractions of substrings). The unescape pass declines a YAML document whose alias refers to its own anchor instead of raising out of the validator. Source offsets survive maqaf detachment on long repetitive text (the sequence matcher no longer discards popular characters as junk).
- A fraction that a percent sign follows (`16 1⁄2%`, `1⁄4%`) is one rate to ground and recall, and the plain percentage matcher no longer takes its denominator as a second one. A fraction-slash run needs a whole numerator (`.5⁄2` and `-.5⁄2` produce no fraction from a decimal's substring). A Hebrew structural reference — a chapter, schedule, part, sign, section, paragraph, table, column, item or regulation named by an ordinal or a number — is no recall obligation, while a substantive ordinal ("the fourth child") still is. Source offsets are recovered by a bounded resynchronising walk across the cleaning pass's local edits, linear on repetitive text, with sequence matching (autojunk on) only for an edit wider than the walk's window.
- Hebrew compound numbers ("twenty and three", "a hundred and twenty", "three hundreds", "two thousand") are one number, and no constituent grounds or is owed on its own. A Hebrew fraction word is a fraction where the grammar says so — a count before it ("two fifths") or no article and a partitive after it ("a fifth of the income") — and "the fourth schedule" keeps its ordinal; half, third and quarter have nouns of their own and are always fractions. A weekday ("יום שני") and a structural reference above ten ("the eleventh chapter", "the twenty-first section") are no recall obligations. Source offsets across the cleaning pass are recovered by a walk that scores each way of passing an edit by how long the texts agree afterwards, so a space inserted every few characters is read as such; one wide edit is passed by bounded local sequence matching.
- The numeric cleaning pass keeps every edit in place — a dropped structural line, a stripped prefix, a detached maqaf, a blanked citation or URL all become spaces of the same width — so a surviving character keeps its own source offset and provenance is the identity on text of any length or repetitiveness; only a pass that inserts a space (a currency glyph detached from its amount) still needs sequence matching. Hebrew numbers spelled with several words are parsed whole by the spoken grammar (thousands, hundreds, tens with a vav-bound unit, teens, a vav-bound fraction: "a hundred and three", "twenty thousand", "one and a half"), a Hebrew percentage word makes its number a rate, a feminine ordinal is a fraction only before "of the", "of" or "מן", and a structural reference accepts every teen spelling the tokenizer does.
- Numeric-extraction provenance is carried through the cleaning edits themselves: every substitution keeps a character's source offset only where that character survives in place, so a currency detachment beside a CRLF, a dropped structural line, a stripped prefix, a rewritten size-cap restatement or a collapsed schedule row can no longer shift or collapse occurrence spans, and line terminators are preserved. Hebrew numerals of several words compose fully (teens before a scale word, hundreds with tens and units, a count of hundreds before a thousand), and a percent word after digits or a fraction slash makes the number a rate.
- A Hebrew teen joined by a hyphen or a maqaf composes inside a larger number ("שנים-עשר אלף" and "שנים־עשר אלף" are 12,000), a percent word after a fraction slash with whitespace around the slash reads the whole fraction as one rate, and a digit percentage keeps its unary minus ("-23 אחוזים" is -0.23).
- A spelling that counts only inside a teen ("שנים", "שתים") is no longer read as a two on its own, so "a hundred years" is 100; the traditional spellings ששה and שלשה count as six and three, alone and inside teens.
- The construct forms "שני" and "שתי" count before a scale word ("שני אלפים" is 2,000), counted fractions accept traditional and construct spellings ("שלשה רבעים", "שלושת רבעי השכר" are 0.75), a structural reference accepts every number-word spelling the parser does, an ASCII fraction before a percent word is one rate ("1/4 אחוזים" is 0.0025), and the compound scan is linear in the length of Hebrew prose.
- An ASCII mixed fraction before a percent word is one rate ("16 1/2 אחוזים" is 0.165), a fraction noun before the percent word is a fraction of a percent ("חמישית אחוז" is 0.002), a mixed number takes a counted fractional tail ("אחד ושני שלישים" is five thirds), a structural reference accepts the whole numeral grammar ("סעיף מאה ועשרים" is a reference, not a 120 to recall), and the compound scan no longer copies the remaining run at each candidate word.
- A count followed by a fraction noun after tens or hundreds is a fractional tail ("עשרים ושלושה רבעים" is 20.75), the percent noun is recognised before its count and in its definite form ("אחוז אחד" is 0.01, "מחצית האחוז" is 0.005), a structural reference takes one number of the grammar and stops before a substantive count, a digit reference covers its list or range ("סעיפים 1 ו־2", "1 עד 3"), and the YAML equivalence check compares alias graphs node-pair by node-pair instead of path by path.
- A Hebrew percentage phrase is read whole with its spelled count and fractional tail ("אחוז וחצי" is 0.015, "שני אחוזים וחצי" is 0.025), a singular structural reference ends at a comma so a following amount stays a recall obligation, a fraction word before a definite noun or after a copula is a fraction ("חמישית ההכנסה", "יהיה חמישית משכרו"), and a structural reference accepts a lone cardinal and a teen after hundreds ("סעיף שלוש", "סעיף מאה ואחד עשר").
- A Hebrew percentage phrase is read whole with a joined teen or printed count and a counted fractional tail ("שנים־עשר אחוזים" is 0.12, "2 אחוזים וחצי" is 0.025, "שני אחוזים ושלושה רבעים" is 0.0275), a fraction word before a definite word is a fraction only after a copula or quantity word so an ordinal before a relative clause stays an ordinal ("דרגה חמישית המקנה"), a plural reference list ends before an amount in any unit (a comma joins non-final items only), a reference composes hundreds without a conjunction ("סעיף מאה עשרים ושלושה"), and the YAML rewrite declines a document its constructor rejects.
- A Hebrew percentage phrase reads a prefixed, grouped, long or negative count whole ("בשני אחוזים וחצי" is 0.025, "1,000 אחוזים וחצי" is 10.005, "מאה עשרים ושלושה ושלושה רבעים אחוזים" is 1.2375, "-2 אחוזים וחצי" is -0.025), a possessive after an ordinal keeps the ordinal ("דרגה חמישית של העובד"), a plural reference list is commas followed by one closing join ("1, 2, 4"; "1 ו־2, 100 או 200 דולר" ends at 2), a reference composes thousands and hundreds without a conjunction, and the parse-once instrumentation test observes the tracked cleaner.
- A standalone carriage return ends a line ("CHAPTER 1\rThe benefit is 100 dollars." keeps its 100 under every profile) while a CRLF keeps its width; a definite ordinal before the percent noun stays an ordinal ("הילד השני אחוז וחצי" is the second child and 0.015); a fractional count is read ("חצי אחוז ורבע" is 0.0075, "שלושה רבעים אחוז" 0.0075); a fraction of a named amount is a fraction after any verb ("ישלם חמישית משכרו" is 0.2) and the negative ordinal cases hold; a comma list ends before a coordinated amount ("1, 2, 4, 100 או 200 דולר" recalls 100 and 200); a range is one list item ("1 עד 3 ו־5"); a spelled reference reads the whole numeral grammar ("סעיף שני אלפים", "פרק שנים עשר אלף"); "שביעית" and "תשיעית" are mixed-number tails; and the percentage pass tokenizes the text once (4,000 phrases in 0.07 s, not 3.8 s).
- A printed fraction count keeps its spelled tail ("1/2 אחוז וחצי" and "1⁄2 אחוז וחצי" are 0.01); a verb beginning with מה is no partitive ("דרגה חמישית מהווה תנאי" keeps its fifth grade); an infinitive payment clause takes a fraction of a named amount ("על המעביד לשלם חמישית השכר" is 0.2); a bare percent noun in a quantity slot with a partitive after it is one percent ("תוספת של אחוז מההכנסה" is 0.01) while "האחוז שנקבע" and "אחוז מסוים" stay unstated; a comma list ends before a range of amounts ("1, 2, 4, 100 עד 200 דולר" recalls 100 and 200); a reference label takes Hebrew subsection letters ("1(א) ו־2(ב)", "5(ב)(2)"); a plural noun heads a list of definite spelled references ("התוספות השלישית והרביעית"); and every backward context search is bounded to the words before its position (4,000 fractions in 0.01 s, not 6 s).
- A prefixed percent noun is still a rate ("באחוז אחד" is 0.01, "באחוז וחצי" 0.015); a reference label is a whole number, so "1, 2, 4, 1,500 עד 2,500 דולר" ends its list at 4 and recalls both amounts; a range of rates shares its percent noun ("בין 2 ל־3 אחוזים" and "בין שניים לשלושה אחוזים" are 0.02 and 0.03); "מה" before a noun after an ordinal is the preposition, not the partitive, unless the clause or the noun says fraction ("לידה חמישית מהיריון נפרד" keeps its fifth birth); !!omap and !!pairs tuples go through the memoized YAML comparison; and the two Hebrew scanning tests time the pass itself, with generous whole-pipeline bounds, so a slower CI runner no longer fails them.
- A range of rates keeps a negative lower endpoint ("-2 עד 3 אחוזים" and "בין -2 ל־3 אחוזים" are -0.02 and 0.03) and reads a fractional one whole ("1/2 עד 3 אחוזים" is 0.005 and 0.03, a number after a slash never being an endpoint of its own); and the unit lexicon that keeps a quantity out of a reference list now covers measures, weights, volumes, energy and counts of people and things, so "סעיפים 1, 2, 4, 100 עד 200 מטרים" recalls both amounts.
- A unit abbreviation is matched with gershayim as well as an ASCII quote ("50 ק״ג" and "100 עד 200 מ״ר" after a reference list stay quantities); the construct cardinal "שני"/"שתי" composes inside a compound ("עשרים ושני הימים" is 22, "מאה ושני הימים" 102) while staying no cardinal on its own or under the article; and a spelled fraction is a range endpoint that shares the percent noun ("בין חצי לשלושה אחוזים" is 0.005 and 0.03, "רבע עד חצי אחוז" 0.0025 and 0.005).
- Feminine and further count nouns mark a quantity after a reference list ("100 עובדות", "50 מבוטחות", "30 נשים", "12 משפחות" stay substantive); a range of rates reads a printed lower endpoint before a ל-prefixed spelled upper one ("בין 2 לשלושה אחוזים" is 0.02 and 0.03) and takes an attached מ prefix as the bound ("משניים לשלושה אחוזים", "מחצי לשלושה אחוזים"); and a construct two before a teen ten ("מאה ושני עשר") is rejected as a number instead of raising, so imperfect source text never crashes extraction.
- A vav-bound count after a percentage is a new quantity ("שלושה אחוזים וחמישה שקלים" is 0.03 and 5); a fractional tail that carries its own unit is not the rate's ("שני אחוזים וחצי שקל" is 0.02 and 0.5); a printed whole with a spelled fractional tail is one count ("3 וחצי אחוזים" is 0.035); a hyphen after a Hebrew prefix is a separator, not a minus ("בין 2 ל-3 אחוזים" is 0.02 and 0.03, "-3 אחוזים" still -0.03); and the unit lexicon takes disability, work-status and institution nouns and derives every masculine plural's construct form ("100 מקבלי קצבאות", "100 עובדי המפעל" stay quantities).
- A hyphen after a Hebrew prefix before a Unicode fraction is a separator, not a minus ("כ-1⁄4 נקודת זיכוי" is 0.25, "-1⁄4" still -0.25); a printed whole with a spelled tail is one range endpoint ("בין 2 וחצי ל־3 וחצי אחוזים" is 0.025 and 0.035); and the unit lexicon takes singular units and count nouns (אגורה, נקודה, שעה, יום, עובד, מבוטח, …), so "שני אחוזים וחצי אגורה" is 0.02 and 0.5.
- A minus after a maqaf is a sign ("כ־−1⁄4" is -0.25, "ב־−2 אחוזים" -0.02) while a hyphen after a letter is still a prefix's; a range's lower bound takes an ASCII hyphen ("מ-2 ל-3 אחוזים" is 0.02 and 0.03); a printed whole with a spelled fractional tail is one quantity anywhere ("3 וחצי נקודות זיכוי" is 3.5, "2 ושלושה רבעים" 2.75); and "שנייה" is the unit of time, not the ordinal, after a fraction, a digit or "כל", or before "אחת" ("חצי שנייה" is 0.5; "לידה שנייה" keeps its 2).
- A percent marker after a mixed number makes it a rate ("3 וחצי%" and "שלושה וחצי%" are 0.035); a fraction word before "שנייה" says unit of time even under the article ("מחצית השנייה" is 0.5), the construct "שניית" is only ever the unit ("כל שניית המתנה"), and a following "אחת" says unit only where the clause before says a quantity follows ("יהיה שנייה אחת" is 1; "דירה שנייה אחת" keeps its second apartment).
- A percent marker after a fraction word is the partitive the percent word is ("חמישית%" is 0.002, "רבע%" 0.0025); a range of rates shares its percent marker as it shares the noun ("בין 2 וחצי ל־3 וחצי%" is 0.025 and 0.035, "2 עד 3%" 0.02 and 0.03); and a prefixed fraction word or a temporal preposition before "שנייה" says unit of time ("לחצי שנייה", "למחצית השנייה" are 0.5; "לאחר שנייה אחת" is 1) while "דירה שנייה אחת" keeps its second apartment.
- A spaced dash is no range join, so a tax schedule row ("על כל שקל חדש מ־84,120 – 10%") keeps its threshold and its rate; a number with a unit after it is a quantity whatever noun precedes it ("תוספת 2 שקלים", "תוספת שתי נקודות זיכוי" are 2) while a schedule reference stays structural; a prefix hyphen before a symbol percentage is no sign ("מ-2 ל-3%" is 0.02 and 0.03, "-3%" still -0.03); a duration limit before "שנייה" says unit of time ("לא יעלה על שנייה אחת" is 1); and the feminine third and quarter ("שלישית", "רביעית") are range endpoints and mixed-number tails like their masculine forms.
- The first item of a reference, printed or spelled, is no half of a coordinated quantity ("תוספת 2 עד 3 שקלים" and "תוספת שתיים עד שלוש נקודות זיכוי" are 2 and 3, while "סעיף 2 עד 3" stays a reference); and a unit after an ordinal-shaped fraction word says fraction ("עשירית שקל" is 0.1, "עשירית שנייה" 0.1, "חמישית נקודת זיכוי" 0.2), while "לידה עשירית" keeps its ordinal.
- A coordinated quantity after a reference noun keeps its lower endpoint when the upper one is a compound or mixed number ("תוספת 2 עד 3 וחצי שקלים" is 2 and 3.5, "2 עד עשרים וחמישה שקלים" 2 and 25); a relational noun after an ordinal-shaped word is no unit of a fraction ("דירה חמישית בת שלושה חדרים" keeps its fifth apartment); and "שניה" is a unit of time like "שנייה" ("עשירית שניה" is 0.1).
- A coordinated quantity after a reference noun keeps its lower endpoint whatever shape the upper one takes ("2 עד 3 1⁄2 שקלים" is 2 and 3.5, "2 עד שלושים ואחד אלף מאתיים ושלושים וחמישה שקלים" 2 and 31,235); and only a unit of measure after an ordinal-shaped word says fraction, so "דרגה חמישית זכאית" and "דרגה חמישית מקבלת" keep their fifth grade while "עשירית שקל" stays a tenth.
- A numerator is no reference label and a standalone fraction is a coordinated endpoint, so "תוספת 1 או 1⁄2 נקודת זיכוי" and "תוספת 2 עד 7⁄2 שקלים" keep both amounts; and a measure noun that opens a temporal phrase is no unit of a fraction ("לידה חמישית שנה לאחר הלידה הקודמת" keeps its fifth birth, "תקופה של חמישית שנה" stays a fifth of a year).
- A bound after a fraction of a unit keeps the fraction ("עשירית שקל לפחות" is 0.1, "חמישית שנה לפחות" 0.2) while a temporal phrase still keeps an ordinal ("לידה חמישית שנה לאחר"); and a coordinated list of amounts after a reference noun keeps every amount however many joins it has ("תוספת 1 או 2 או 3 שקלים" and "תוספת 1, 2 או 3 שקלים" are 1, 2 and 3).
- The coordinated-quantity guards are deterministic (every token has one role, so a run of vav-bound number words no longer backtracks exponentially); a spelled comma list of amounts after a singular noun keeps every amount ("תוספת שתיים, שלוש או ארבע נקודות זיכוי"); a percentage is shared across every alternative ("1 או 2 או 3 אחוזים" and "1, 2 או 3 אחוזים" are 0.01, 0.02 and 0.03); and a temporal phrase after a unit keeps an ordinal only where no clause context says a quantity follows ("עשירית שקל לאחר הגשת הבקשה" is 0.1).
- The coordinated-quantity guards read each endpoint with the numeral grammar inside an atomic group, so teens ("שלושה עשר"), compounds ("עשרים ואחד") and spelled conjunctions ("שתיים ושלוש") are read once and never re-partitioned; only the supplement noun "תוספת" takes the comma-allowed list of amounts, so "סעיף 5, 2 או 3 אחוזים" keeps section 5; the percentage walk-back stops before a section, an age or a year ("לילד עד גיל 5, 2 או 3 אחוזים" keeps the age); and only a unit of time opens a temporal phrase, so "עשירית שקל לאחר הגשת הבקשה" is a tenth of a shekel in any wording.
- The percentage walk-back stops at a structural reference span rather than a noun list, so "לפי סעיף קטן 5, 2 או 3 אחוזים" keeps subsection 5 while "תוספת 1, 2 או 3 אחוזים" shares the noun across every amount; a coordinated endpoint reads a counted fraction before a bare count and a full multiplier before אלף ("1 או שלושה רבעים נקודת זיכוי", "2 עד מאה ועשרים אלף שקלים" keep both amounts); a vav join shares the percent noun without a bound ("2 ו־3 אחוזים, בהתאמה", "שניים ושלושה אחוזים" are 0.02 and 0.03); and a fractional duration before a temporal phrase is an ordinal only with evidence of one, a noun the ordinal modifies ("המכשיר יופעל עשירית שנייה לאחר קבלת האות" is 0.1).
- Any feminine noun before an ordinal-shaped fraction word is evidence of the ordinal ("בדיקה חמישית שנה לאחר" keeps its fifth examination while "יופעל עשירית שנייה לאחר" stays a tenth of a second); a cited or prefixed "תוספת" is a schedule reference ("לפי תוספת 5, 2 או 3 אחוזים" keeps schedule 5) while a bare one before a list of amounts is a supplement; a percentage is shared across every vav join ("1 ו־2 ו־3 אחוזים", "אחד ושניים ושלושה אחוזים"); and a coordinated endpoint may carry a numeral prefix ("2 עד כשלושה שקלים", "2 עד כ-3 שקלים" keep both amounts).
- A verb-shaped word before an ordinal-shaped fraction word is no evidence of an ordinal ("ממתינה עשירית שנייה לאחר", "ישהה עשירית שנייה לאחר" stay a tenth of a second); a prefixed "תוספת" is a supplement, not a schedule ("בתוספת 1, 2 או 3 אחוזים" shares the noun across every amount) while a cited, definite, or "to the law" schedule stays one and the citation words match across any short whitespace ("לפי  תוספת 5"); and the percentage walk-back crosses an ASCII-hyphen vav join ("1 ו-2 ו-3 אחוזים").
- A verb that governs a duration before an ordinal-shaped fraction word says duration whatever its ending ("תשהה עשירית שנייה", "המתינה עשירית שנייה" are a tenth of a second) while any other word ending in ה or ת is a noun the ordinal modifies ("מרפאה חמישית שנה לאחר" keeps its fifth clinic); and a citation word before a schedule ("לפי", "בהתאם ל", "כאמור ב", …) joins the reference match across any whitespace, so "בהתאם  לתוספת 5, 2 או 3 אחוזים" keeps schedule 5.
- An ordinal-shaped fraction word before a time unit and a temporal phrase is read by evidence, not by word endings: a listed noun before it says ordinal, a duration verb (with a conjunction prefix or not) says duration, and otherwise the unit decides, a fraction of a second, minute or hour being a duration ("פעלה עשירית שנייה לאחר") and a fifth something a year or month after being an ordinal ("מרפאה חמישית שנה לאחר"); and a citation word's internal whitespace is free ("על  פי תוספת 5" keeps schedule 5).
- An ordinal-shaped fraction word before a time unit and a temporal phrase that nothing in the text settles ("מרפאה חמישית שנה לאחר", "נעדר חמישית שנה לאחר") is recorded with both readings, the ordinal and the fraction, so either grounds and the recall obligation is met by either; and the numeral grammar composes millions and billions with construct counts and scaled fractional tails ("שלושה מיליון" is 3,000,000, "מיליון וחצי" 1,500,000, "אלף וחצי" 1,500).
- The numeral grammar reads scale words through their prefixes ("בכמיליון" no longer raises KeyError), composes descending scales ("מיליארד ומאתיים מיליון" is 1,200,000,000; "שני מיליארד ושלוש מאות מיליון ומאתיים אלף" is 2,300,200,000), accepts construct plurals ("שלושה מיליוני שקלים"), and reads a printed multiplier with a Hebrew scale word as one amount ("3.5 מיליון" is 3,500,000; "2 אלף" 2,000; "3 וחצי מיליון" 3,500,000); and an ordinal-shaped fraction word before a time unit reads as a duration, with no ordinal alternative, when the word before it is not feminine-singular shaped ("העובדים נעדרו חמישית שנה", "העובד נעדר חמישית שנה").
- A printed multiplier's scale word carries no prefix, so "בין 3 למיליון" grounds both endpoints of the range and not 3,000,000; a printed multiplier composes with a scaled tail and with descending spelled scales ("3 מיליון וחצי" is 3,500,000; "3 מיליון ומאתיים אלף" 3,200,000); a fractional or mixed multiplier reads with its scale ("חצי מיליון" is 500,000; "שלושה וחצי מיליון" 3,500,000); the construct thousand counts its multiplier ("שלושת אלפי השקלים" is 3,000); and an ordinal-shaped fraction word after an irregular feminine noun ("קרן", "עיר", "דרך") keeps both readings instead of collapsing to a duration.
- A printed multiplier's scaled tail is a whole fraction word ("3 מיליון וחציון" no longer invents 3,500,000), a printed fraction multiplies its scale word ("1⁄2 מיליון" and "1⁄ 2 מיליון" are 500,000; "2 1⁄2 מיליון" 2,500,000), a counted fraction multiplies its scale word ("שלושת רבעי מיליון" is 750,000), and a fraction word after a scale word that names its own operand is no scaled tail: "3 מיליון וחמישית מההכנסה" grounds 3,000,000 and 0.2, "3 מיליון וחצי אלף" is 3,000,500.
- A printed fraction with a zero denominator before a scale word no longer aborts extraction; a fraction word after a scale word keeps its own operand on grammatical grounds, so "3 מיליון וחמישית ההכנסה" grounds 3,000,000 and 0.2 while "3 מיליון וחצי משולם לעובד" stays 3,500,000; and a mixed multiplier with a counted fractional tail scales ("3 ושלושה רבעים מיליון" and "שלושה ושלושה רבעים מיליון" are 3,750,000).
- The partitive grammar names budgets, expenses, turnover, debts, loans and other amounts ("3 מיליון וחצי מהתקציב" grounds 3,000,000 and 0.5), a counted fractional tail keeps its own operand and otherwise scales with the scale word before it ("שלושה מיליון ושני שלישים מההכנסה" is 3,000,000 and two thirds; "מיליון ושני שלישים" is 1,666,666.67), and printed lower-scale remainders compose ("3 מיליון ו־200 אלף" is 3,200,000; "3 מיליארד ו־200 מיליון ו־50 אלף" 3,200,050,000).
- An amount noun's plural possessive ending is read in the partitive grammar ("3 מיליון וחצי מהכנסותיהם" grounds 3,000,000 and 0.5), a spelled amount composes with printed remainders ("שלושה מיליון ו־200 אלף" is 3,200,000; "3 מיליון ו־200 שקלים" 3,000,200), the endpoints of a range share a trailing scale word ("בין 3 ל־5 מיליון" and "שלושה עד חמישה מיליון" run from 3,000,000 to 5,000,000, while "בין 3 למיליון" stays apart), and a scale word before "ו־20 אחוזים" is no longer read as a million-percent lower bound.
- A shared-scale range keeps a signed lower endpoint ("בין -3 ל־5 מיליון" runs from −3,000,000) and reads compound spelled endpoints ("עשרים ושלושה עד שלושים מיליון" runs from 23,000,000), a labelling noun before the lower endpoint shares nothing ("תוספת 2 עד מאה ועשרים אלף" is supplement 2, up to 120,000), and a spelled percentage after a scaled amount keeps the amount ("3 מיליון ועשרים אחוזים" is 3,000,000 and twenty percent).
- A fraction or count before a percent noun or sign counts a rate and is no tail or remainder of the scaled amount before it ("3 מיליון וחצי אחוז" is 3,000,000 and half a percent; "3 מיליון ועשרים%" 3,000,000 and twenty percent), and a shared-scale range reads mixed endpoints ("בין 2 וחצי ל־3 מיליון" runs from 2,500,000).
- A multiword rate before a percent sign leaves the scaled amount before it whole ("שלושה מיליון ועשרים וחמישה%" is 3,000,000 and twenty-five percent; "3 מיליון ושלושה רבעים%" 3,000,000 and three quarters of a percent), and a shared-scale range reads a fractional lower endpoint ("בין חצי ל־3 מיליון" runs from 500,000).
- A mixed rate after a spelled scaled amount keeps the amount's scale ("שלושה מיליון ושלושה וחצי אחוזים" is 3,000,000 and 3.5 percent; "ושלושה ושלושה רבעים אחוזים" likewise), and a shared-scale range reads a ל prefix on a spelled upper endpoint under "בין" or "מ־" ("בין שלושה לחמישה מיליון" runs from 3,000,000 to 5,000,000).
- A printed mixed rate after a scaled amount keeps the amount ("3 מיליון ו־3 וחצי אחוזים" is 3,000,000 and 3.5 percent; "ו־3 ושלושה רבעים%" likewise), and a shared-scale range reads a מ prefix attached to a spelled lower endpoint as the bound ("משלושה לחמישה מיליון" runs from 3,000,000; "מחצי לשלושה מיליון" from 500,000).
- A printed remainder after a scaled amount is read whole before its marker: "3 מיליון ו־3 1/2 אחוזים" is 3,000,000 and 3.5 percent (also with a fraction slash or a percent sign), while "3 מיליון ו־3 וחצי שקלים" and "3 מיליון ו־3 1/2 שקלים" are 3,000,003.5.
- A bare printed fraction after a scaled amount is read whole whatever the spacing around its slash ("3 מיליון ו־1 / 2 אחוזים" is 3,000,000 and half a percent; "3 מיליון ו־1 / 2 שקלים" 3,000,000.5), a fraction before a percent sign is one rate ("1/2%" is half a percent, not two), and a fraction's denominator before the sign is never a rate of its own.
- A remainder after a scaled amount composes only where no separate quantity follows: "3 מיליון ו־30 ימי מאסר" is a fine of 3,000,000 and thirty days, "3 מיליון ו־20 עובדים" a turnover of 3,000,000 and twenty workers, while "3 מיליון ו־200 שקלים" stays 3,000,200; printed and spelled alike.
- A unit after a remainder names a separate quantity only in a money context: "קנס של 3 מיליון ו־30 ימי מאסר" is a fine of 3,000,000 and thirty days, "קנס של 3 מיליון וחצי שנת מאסר" 3,000,000 and half a year, "מחזור של 3 מיליון ו־2 אלף עובדים" 3,000,000 and two thousand workers, while "מרחק של שלושה אלפים ומאתיים מטרים" is 3,200 metres and "עשרת אלפים וחמש מאות תושבים" 10,500 residents.
- An amount noun makes a number money only where it governs it, through connectors alone ("קנס של", "מחזור שנתי של", "הקנס לא יעלה על"): "המענק יינתן למפעל המעסיק לפחות שלושה אלפים ומאתיים עובדים" is a threshold of 3,200 workers. A separate quantity is read whole before any of it composes: "מחזור של שלושה מיליון ושני אלפים וחמש מאות עובדים" and "מחזור של 3 מיליון ו־2 אלף ו־500 עובדים" are 3,000,000 and 2,500 workers.
- A lower-scale quantity after a money amount is read through its printed continuation before any of it composes ("מחזור של שלושה מיליון ושני אלפים ו־500 עובדים" is 3,000,000 and 2,500 workers), and a construct chain qualifies the amount noun that binds the number ("מחזור העסקאות השנתי של 3 מיליון ו־20 עובדים" is 3,000,000 and twenty workers).
- One articled possessor may qualify the amount noun that binds a number ("מחזור העסקאות", "הכנסת המפעל"), while a relative participle after it ("המפעל המעסיק לפחות 3 אלפים ו־200 עובדים") opens a clause of its own and binds nothing, so the worker threshold reads 3,200.
- A dative ל names whom an amount is for, not its amount: "תקציב המיועד ל־3 אלפים ו־200 עובדים" and "תקציב המיועד לשלושה אלפים ומאתיים עובדים" are a budget intended for 3,200 workers, and the count reads whole; "תקציב ב־3 מיליון ו־20 עובדים" still binds the money.
- An articled possessor qualifies the amount noun only where "של", an adjective, a copula or a threshold phrase follows it; a participle with a prepositional complement ("הקצבה המחולקת בין 3 אלפים ו־200 עובדים", an allocation distributed among 3,200 workers) opens a clause of its own, and the count reads whole.
- After a possessor of the amount noun, the way on to the number carries no bare preposition however many modifiers intervene: "הקצבה המחולקת לכל היותר בין 3 אלפים ו־200 עובדים" is an allocation distributed among at most 3,200 workers, and the count reads whole; "הקנס יהיה לכל היותר בין 3 ל־5 מיליון" still binds the money.
- An amount noun takes a possessor only in the construct state: "סכום המענק" and "הכנסת המפעל" bind the number through the possessor, while an articled amount noun followed by an articled word ("המענק המממן לפחות 3 אלפים ו־200 עובדים", a grant financing at least 3,200 workers) is attribution, so the clause binds nothing and the count reads whole.
- "כולל" is read as the adjective "total" only where "של", a copula or another adjective follows it ("המחזור הכולל של 3 מיליון"), and as the verb "includes" otherwise, so what it includes is a count of its own: "הסיוע כולל 3 אלפים ו־200 מיטות" is assistance including 3,200 beds.
- A bare dual scales its fractional tail by the thousand ("אלפיים וחצי" is 2,500, as "שני אלפים וחצי" is), and "כולל" is the adjective "total" before a threshold predicate alone ("הכולל לא יעלה על"), the verb "includes" before "לא פחות מ־" and the like, so "הסיוע כולל לא פחות מ־3 אלפים ו־200 מיטות" counts 3,200 beds.
- A percent noun or sign right after a printed scale amount, or after the scale word a range's endpoints share, makes the value a rate before its span is reserved: "3 אלפים אחוזים" is 30, as "שלושת אלפים אחוזים" is, and "2 עד 3 אלפים אחוזים" runs from 20 to 30.
- A scaled percentage keeps its fractional tail in both forms ("3 אלפים אחוזים וחצי" and "שלושת אלפים אחוזים וחצי" are 3,000.5 percent), a scaled count before the percent noun is the rate's own unless a money amount governs it ("שלושת אלפים אחוזים" is 3,000 percent; "סכום של שלושה מיליון ועשרים אחוזים" stays three million and twenty percent), and a printed multiplier's scale word before the noun is read by the printed pass, never as a count of one.
- A fractional tail after a percent unit that carries a unit of its own stays that unit's ("3 אלפים אחוזים וחצי שקל" is 30 and half a shekel), and a scaled percentage with a remainder is one rate outside a money context ("3 אלפים וחמש מאות אחוזים", "שלושת אלפים וחמש מאות%" and "3 אלפים ו־200%" are 3,500 and 3,200 percent), while under a money amount the remainder before the percent unit stays a rate of its own.
- A scaled percentage reads as one rate in every form: a printed or spelled leading amount, a spelled, printed or mixed remainder, the percent noun or the sign, and a fractional tail of the rate's own or of another unit ("שלושת אלפים ו־200 אחוזים" is 3,200 percent; "3 אלפים ו־200 וחצי אחוזים" 3,200.5 percent; "שלושת אלפים% וחצי" 3,000.5 percent), with the seventy combinations covered by one regression.
- A printed fraction that continues a scaled percentage is read with the whole ("שלושת אלפים ו־200 1/2 אחוזים וחצי" is 3,200.51 percent), the scaled-percentage grid grows to 98 cells, and the continuation check reuses one token index per pass, so a document of thousands of scaled percentages scans in linear time.
- A percent sign carries its fractional tail on plain printed and singleton spelled counts ("3% וחצי" and "שלושה% וחצי" are 3.5 percent), a hundreds remainder leaves room for a printed remainder below it ("3 אלפים ומאה ו־20" is 3,120), a negative mixed count signs the whole rate ("-3 וחצי אחוזים וחצי" is minus four percent), and an explicit range scales a thousand-plus lower endpoint as a rate ("בין 1,000 ל־2,000 אחוזים" runs from ten percent).
- A printed mixed count carries the fractional tail after its percent sign ("3 וחצי% וחצי" is four percent, the sign applied last), a range of rates reads endpoints that each carry a printed multiplier and scale word ("בין 3 אלפים ל־4 אלפים אחוזים" runs from thirty to forty), descending spelled components follow a printed remainder ("3 אלפים ו־100 ועשרים" is 3,120), and the printed-scale pass indexes its spelled neighbours and occupied spans so thousands of mixed-scale amounts scan in linear time.
- A continuation after a scaled amount is read whole before it is judged, so a separate quantity or a rate after it takes all of it ("קנס של 3 אלפים ו־100 ועשרים ימי מאסר" is a 3,000 fine and 120 days) and descending components continue until the amount ends ("3 אלפים ו־100 ועשרים ו־3" is 3,123); a shared-scale range's lower endpoint that is already a complete amount shares nothing ("בין 3 אלפים ומאה ל־4 אלפים" runs from 3,100); a range of rates reads any complete printed amount as an endpoint, mixed multipliers and remainders included ("בין 3 וחצי אלפים ל־4 אלפים אחוזים" runs from thirty-five); and a printed multiplier's tail and scale word before a percent noun are the printed pass's rate, not a phrase of their own ("4 וחצי אלפים אחוזים" is forty-five).
- A range's lower endpoint that continues a scaled amount through any number of vav-bound components shares nothing with the upper scale ("בין 3 אלפים ומאה ו־20 ל־4 אלפים" runs from 3,120), a percent unit after a whole continuation makes all of it one rate of its own under a money amount ("סכום של 3 אלפים ו־100 ועשרים אחוזים" is 3,000 and 120 percent), a percent phrase whose count continues a scaled amount is left to the printed pass, and a shared-scale range's unit is read after the whole upper endpoint, remainder included ("בין 2 ל־3 אלפים ומאתיים אחוזים" runs from twenty).
- One continuation reader now serves every pass: after a scaled amount, printed lower scales, printed remainders and spelled remainders are read in any order until the amount ends, then judged once ("סכום של 3 מיליון ו־2 אלף אחוזים" is three million and 2,000 percent; "סכום של שלושת אלפים ומאה ו־20 אחוזים" three thousand and 120 percent); the shared-scale range's unit is read after the whole upper endpoint including printed lower scales ("בין 2 ל־3 מיליון ו־200 אלף אחוזים" runs from 20,000 percent); and the range guard's walk back crosses multiword spelled components ("בין 3 אלפים וחמש מאות ו־20 ל־4 אלפים" runs from 3,520).
- A percent phrase whose count opens a scaled amount's continuation carrying a scale word of its own is left whole to the continuation reader ("סכום של 3 מיליון ושני אלפים וחמש מאות אחוזים" is three million and 25 percent, not 2,000 and five), and a range of rates parses a spelled lower endpoint before judging its scale, so a remainder after the scale word no longer hides it ("בין שלושת אלפים ומאה ל־4 אלפים אחוזים" runs from 31 percent).
- A grouped or thousand-plus printed lower bound is a complete amount that shares no scale word ("בין 2,000 ל־3 אלפים שקלים" runs from 2,000, not two million), a range of rates reads scale from the parser's own classification so a scaled numeral such as אלפיים shares the percent unit, the percent phrase pass judges a printed multiplier by the count's own head rather than the run's first word ("2 אלפים עד שלושת אלפים ומאה אחוזים" keeps its upper endpoint), and a unary sign before a spelled or fractional count signs the rate ("−חצי אחוז" is minus half a percent).
- A thousand-plus printed lower bound is a complete amount whatever the upper endpoint's scale ("בין 1500 ל־3 מיליון" runs from 1,500, grouped or not), a unary sign before a spelled count the percent sign marks signs the rate ("−שלושה%" is minus three percent, "−חצי%" minus half), and signed spelled range endpoints keep their sign in value and span, the bound and the join read past the sign ("−שלושה עד שלושה אחוזים" runs from minus three, "בין −חצי ל־3 אחוזים" from minus half).
- A unary sign before any spelled number signs it, percent-marked or not ("−שלושה מיליון שקלים" is minus three million, "−חצי שקל" minus half a shekel), a signed spelled upper endpoint no longer hides a shared-scale range's join ("−שלושה עד −שניים אלפים אחוזים" runs from minus thirty to minus twenty), and a shared scale word reaches every earlier alternative in a list ("1, 2 או 3 מיליון" is one, two and three million).
- A negative spelled leading amount keeps its sign when composed with printed lower scales or remainders ("−שלושה מיליון ו־200 אלף" is minus 3,200,000, "−אלפיים ו־300" minus 2,300), and a list that shares a scale word closes with a vav conjunction as well as with "או" ("1, 2 ו־3 מיליון" and "אחד, שניים ושלושה מיליון" are one, two and three million).
- A shared-scale list whose conjunctions are attached to the spelled amounts is scaled throughout ("אחד ושניים ושלושה מיליון" is one, two and three million; "אחד ושניים ושלושה אלפים אחוזים" ten, twenty and thirty percent), the walk back reading a vav on the endpoint itself as the percent-range walk does.
- A count that opens the next counted hundreds is no remainder of the hundreds before it ("מאתיים ושלוש מאות" is two hundred and three hundred, two amounts, while "מאתיים ושלוש" stays 203), and a comma-only list shares its scale word or percent unit throughout ("1, 2, 3 מיליון" is one, two and three million; "1, 2, 3 אחוזים" one, two and three percent), a reference or a label before the lower endpoint keeping it apart.
- A comma join in a list of rates or shared-scale amounts applies only where a Hebrew word anchors the list, so English currency and age operands before a comma stay what they are ("For income up to $500, 10% applies" keeps 500; "under age 5, 3%" keeps the age), and tens no longer absorb a count that opens counted hundreds or a well-formed teen of its own ("שלושים וארבע מאות" is thirty and four hundred, "עשרים ושלושה עשר" twenty and thirteen), while "מאה ואחד עשר" stays 111 and a malformed teen stays no teen.
- A comma before the upper endpoint of a list of rates or shared-scale amounts counts only with positive evidence of a list, an earlier item before the lower endpoint or "בהתאמה" after the unit, so a lone comma separating clauses leaves a threshold or an age what it is ("על הכנסה עד 500, 10% מס" keeps 500, "לילד שגילו 5, 3%" keeps the age) while "1, 2, 3 אחוזים" and "2, 3 מיליון שקלים, בהתאמה" still share.
- A comma joins a list of rates or shared-scale amounts only when "בהתאמה" follows the unit ("1, 2, 3 אחוזים, בהתאמה"); an earlier range or alternative before the comma is no evidence, so "על הכנסה של 100 עד 500, 10% מס" keeps its thresholds and "לילד שגילו 4 או 5, 3%" its ages, a spelled operand before the comma is judged as a printed one is ("עד חמש מאות, 3 מיליון" keeps 500), and a label with a possessive suffix ("שגילו 5") stops the walk back as the bare label does.
- A walk back over a list of rates or shared-scale amounts crosses a comma only to an item that is no threshold of its own: under "בהתאמה" always, otherwise only when a Hebrew word that is no limit governor ("עד", "מעל", "בסך", "מ־" and the like) anchors the item, so "על הכנסה עד 500, 2 או 3% מס" keeps its threshold, printed or spelled, while "שיעור המס יהיה 1, 2 או 3 אחוזים" still lists three rates.
- A comma joins a list of rates or shared-scale amounts, and a walk back crosses one, only to an item of a list a predicate introduces ("הם", "יהיה", "כדלקמן:", a supplement noun), reached directly or through earlier items; a threshold before a comma keeps its value whatever governs it ("על הכנסה שאינה עולה על 500, 2 או 3% מס" keeps 500, printed or spelled), and "בהתאמה" after the unit is no longer taken as evidence, since it governs the rates alone.
- Only a plural predicate or an explicit introducer anchors a comma-joined list of rates or shared-scale amounts ("השיעורים הם 1, 2, 3 אחוזים", "שיעורי המס יהיו 1, 2 או 3 אחוזים", "כדלקמן: 1, 2 או 3 אחוזים", a supplement noun); a singular copula states one value, so a condition with the same shape keeps it ("אם ההכנסה היא 500, 2 או 3% ממנה" keeps 500, "אם גילו הוא 5, 2 או 3%" keeps the age, printed or spelled).
- A comma never joins a list of rates or shared-scale amounts, in the initial join or in the walk back over earlier alternatives: it separates clauses as often as it lists, and nothing in the text tells the two apart, so a threshold, an age or a condition before a comma keeps its value ("על הכנסה עד 500, 10% מס" keeps 500, "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3% מהם" keeps 500). A list a conjunction closes shares from the joined pair on ("1 או 2 או 3 אחוזים", "1 ו־2 ו־3 מיליון" share throughout; "1, 2 או 3 אחוזים" shares the two and the three).
- An operand that carries a currency mark of its own, a sign before it or a currency word or sign after it, shares no percent unit and no scale word whatever join follows it ("הקנס יהיה $500 או 2% מהמחזור" keeps 500, "הסכום הוא בין ₪ 500 ל־3 מיליון שקלים" keeps 500), in both range passes and their walks back.
- A bare vav pair shares a percent unit or a scale word only under "בהתאמה" after the unit, the marker of a paired list ("2 ו־3 אחוזים, בהתאמה", "1 ו־2 ו־3 מיליון שקלים, בהתאמה"); without it the vav joins clauses as often ("מספר העובדים הוא 50 ו־10% מהם זכאים" keeps 50, "ההכנסה היא 500 ו־2% ממנה" keeps 500), and a currency code before or after an operand ("USD 500", "500 EUR"), at any spacing, marks it an amount as a sign does.
- A walk back over earlier alternatives crosses a vav only under "בהתאמה" after the unit, as the initial vav pair does ("ההכנסה היא 500 ו־2 או 3% ממנה" keeps 500), "ועד" is read as the range connector it is ("מ־2 ועד 3 אחוזים" runs from two), a currency mark counts however wide the gap or whatever bidirectional formatting stands between it and the amount, a bidirectional mark before a digit becomes the space it stands for, and a shekel sign glued to its amount ("₪500") is detached as the cedi sign is.
- A currency mark counts across any whitespace, a newline or a thin space included, and every bidirectional control, and "בהתאמה" describes the pair it follows, not a value a singular copula states before the vav ("ההכנסה היא 500 ו־2 או 3% ממנה ינוכו ליחיד ולחברה, בהתאמה" keeps 500), while a plural copula still introduces the list ("הסכומים הם 1 ו־2 או 3 מיליון שקלים, בהתאמה").
- A list of rates or shared-scale amounts keeps one conjunction, so a walk back crosses only joins of the kind its pair started with ("1 או 2 או 3 אחוזים" and "1 ו־2 ו־3 מיליון, בהתאמה" share throughout; "500 ו־2 או 3%" is a clause and a pair, and the 500 stays), a modifier may stand between a singular copula and the value it states ("ההכנסה היא בדיוק 500"), and every currency marker the pipeline already knows, with the shekel sign and the ILS, NIS and JPY codes, denominates an operand ("CAD 500 או 2%", "בין ¥ 500 ל־3 מיליון").
- A vav never joins a list of rates or shared-scale amounts, in the initial pair or in the walk back: the vav-paired list does not occur in the statute text these passes serve, and the same vav joins clauses ("ההכנסה עומדת על 500 ו־2 ו־3% ממנה ינוכו" keeps 500), so the "בהתאמה", copula and conjunction-kind rules of rounds 92 to 95 are gone with it; an "או" alternative that a comparison follows ("500 או 2% מהמחזור, לפי הגבוה") or that opens with a bare hundred-plus number shares no percent unit, while "או" lists and bounded ranges share as before.
- An "או" alternative that a singular money noun governs directly is one amount beside the other ("קנס של 50 או 2% מהמחזור" keeps 50, "סכום של 500 או 3 מיליון" keeps 500), a rate word before the alternatives makes them a list of rates however large ("בשיעור של 125 או 150 אחוזים" is 125 and 150 percent), and the hundred-plus rule of the previous round, which misread that overtime form, is gone.
- An "או" alternative shares a percent unit only under an explicit rate word before the pair ("בשיעור של 125 או 150 אחוזים", "שיעור המס יהיה 2 או 3 אחוזים", "תוספת 1 או 2 אחוזים"); without one the number before "או" keeps its value ("קנס של 50 או 2% מהמחזור", "הקנס יהיה 50 או 2%"), and an "או" alternative never shares a scale word ("הקנס הוא 500 או 3 מיליון" keeps 500), so the comparison, money-noun and magnitude rules of the two previous rounds are gone; bounded and explicit ranges remain.
- A unit word distributes over "או" and a sign or a bare scale word does not: "125 או 150 אחוזים" and "2 או 3 מיליון שקלים" share their unit, "50 או 2%" and "500 או 3 מיליון" keep the number before "או", a rate word in the same clause makes a signed pair share ("בשיעור של 2 או 3%"), a range must ascend ("בין 500 ל־3 מיליון" runs from 500 shekels), and "תוספת" is no rate word.
- A decreasing range is a range ("יופחת מ־5 ל־3 אחוזים" runs from five to three percent) and only a "בין" range must ascend, a comma ends the clause a rate word governs, and a vav pair shares its unit under a plural heading and "בהתאמה" ("שיעורי המס הם 2 ו־3 אחוזים, בהתאמה", "הסכומים הם 2 ו־3 מיליון שקלים, בהתאמה") while a singular predicate before the vav keeps its value ("ההכנסה עומדת על 500 ו־2 ו־3%").
- A vav pair shares its unit under a plural noun of the unit's kind heading the clause, with or without "בהתאמה" ("שיעורי המס הם 2 ו־3 אחוזים" lists two rates, "הסכומים הם 2 ו־3 מיליון שקלים" two amounts), a bare plural copula is no such noun ("ההכנסות הן 500 ו־2 ו־3% מהן" keeps 500), and a colon-terminated currency heading ("הסכומים בשקלים:") denominates the bare numbers of the clauses after it, so "הקנס יהיה 50 או 2 אחוזים" under it keeps 50 while a rate word still makes a pair rates.
- A spelled three-item rate list no longer crashes the walk back; a coordinated list is headed by a plural noun of the unit's kind as the subject of the copula or construct right before it ("שיעורי המס הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים" lists three rates, commas and vavs within it joining), while a noun governing another predicate heads nothing ("שיעורי המס יחולו על הכנסה של 500 ו־2 ו־3%" keeps 500) and a conditional clause states a condition ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3%" keeps 500).
- A list heading governs only the list body right after it, so a heading completed earlier in the clause leaves a later predicate alone ("שיעורי המס הם 10% ו־20%, הקנס יהיה 50 ו־2%" keeps the fine at 50), any connector joins within a headed list ("שיעורי המס הם 10, 20 או 30 אחוזים" lists three rates), and the colon that introduces a list ("השיעורים כדלקמן: 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים") no longer cuts the heading off.
- A conditional clause is recognised after a sentence stop, a list heading's body is validated whole so prose in any script between the heading and the number ends its reach, a decimal point and the colon after a list copula are no clause stops ("שיעורי המס הם 10.5, 20 ו־30 אחוזים", "השיעורים הם: 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים"), and inside a verified heading the percent-sign, bare-scale and thousand-value guards stand down ("שיעורי המס הם 10, 20 או 30%", "הסכומים הם 10, 20 ו־30 מיליון", "השיעורים הם 1000, 2000 ו־3000 אחוזים" share throughout).
- A conditional marker anywhere before a list heading, after a preamble or with a vav ("לעניין זה, כאשר התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון"), keeps the condition's number; a heading admits only a definite complement between the plural noun and its copula, so another predicate is never swallowed ("הקנסות ייגזרו מתשלום של 500, 2 או 3 מיליון" keeps 500); and inside a verified heading thousand-plus and grouped multipliers share the scale ("הסכומים הם 900, 1000 ו־1100 מיליון שקלים").
- The construct nouns of the unit's kind stand in a list heading whether or not they are definite ("שיעורי דמי הביטוח הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים" reads three rates); a condition closed before the heading's own comma segment leaves the list headed ("אם ההכנסה נמוכה, השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים"); a line wrap after a comma, a join or the copula is whitespace inside a headed list ("הסכומים הם 1,\n2 ו־3 מיליון שקלים"); and under a heading the percentage pass leaves a thousand-plus or grouped multiplier to the shared-scale pass ("השיעורים הם 900, 1000 ו־1100 אלפים אחוזים" reads 9,000, 10,000 and 11,000).
- Before a true copula the whole subject phrase heads a list ("שיעורי מס ערך מוסף הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים", "הסכומים ששולמו לעובדים הם 1, 2 ו־3 מיליון שקלים"), while before "של" only a nominal chain does; an indented line wrap inside a headed list is whitespace; and a list lying wholly within a condition is headed ("אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים בהתאמה, תחול ההוראה"), where a clause running on past the unit into the consequent still crosses a clause transition.
- Within a condition a modifier of the unit before the comma belongs to the list ("אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים מההכנסה, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; "שקלים חדשים," three amounts) while a verb running on is still the consequent; the subject phrase before a true copula runs to the copula within the clause, numbers included ("השיעורים שנקבעו בצו שר האוצר הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים"); and a signed number after a line wrap continues a headed list ("השיעורים הם 10,\n  -20 ו־30 אחוזים").
- Within a condition the whole modifier phrase of the unit belongs to the list ("אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים מההכנסה החייבת, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; "שקלים חדשים לשנת המס," three amounts); a parenthetical or an attached subsection marker in the subject phrase keeps the heading ("השיעורים שנקבעו בצו (להלן הצו) הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים", "השיעורים לפי סעיף 2(א) הם"); and a signed number word after a line wrap continues a headed list ("השיעורים הם 10,\n  -עשרים ו־30 אחוזים").
- The whole number of a mixed fraction stands on the fraction's own line ("10\n\n1⁄4" is ten, then a quarter); within a condition a future verb or a plural participle after the unit is the clause running on while an adjective, a construct noun or a relative clause modifies the unit ("אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים מהכנסה חייבת, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; "שקלים משולמים כמענק" heads nothing); a colon inside a subject parenthetical is no clause stop ("בצו (להלן: הצו) הם"); and a no-break or em space indents a wrapped list like an ASCII space.
- Within a condition a word ending in ים, ות or ת after the unit is an adjective or a noun, never a future verb, so "אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים נוספים, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; Hebrew number words never compose across a paragraph boundary ("שלושה\n\nעשר" is three, then ten) while a single line wrap still joins them; and a mixed fraction's whole number is joined to it by a space of some width only, never a Unicode paragraph, line or page separator.
- Within a condition the comma after the condition, a clause separator or a list tail closes a headed list whatever words modify the unit ("אם השיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים מהכנסה נמוכה, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; "שקלים מסוימים, ישולם מענק" three amounts), while a sentence ending with words between and no comma, or a plural future verb, is the consequent running on ("שקלים משולמים כמענק." heads nothing); a percentage's spelled number ends at a paragraph boundary ("שלושה\n\nעשר אחוזים" is three, then ten percent); and every mixed-fraction reader joins a whole number to its fraction by a space of some width only ("10\n\n1⁄4 מיליון" is ten, then a quarter of a million).
- Within a condition only the word right after the unit is read for verb shape, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים ישלם המעסיק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500 while "אחוזים מההכנסה נטו, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; and a spelled tail or a printed remainder joins its number across a space or a single line wrap only, never a blank line or a paragraph separator ("10\n\nוחצי מיליון" is ten, then half a million).
- Within a condition the consequent's verb is read after a modifier too, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים חדשים ישלם המעסיק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500 while "אחוזים ממס ישיר, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; a ת-final verb such as "ישית" counts; and a scale word or a percent noun joins a printed number across a space or a single line wrap only ("10\n\nמיליון" is ten, then a million).
- Within a condition, agreement tells an adjective from the consequent's verb: an adjective agrees with the noun before it in gender and number ("אחוזים מהכנסה יומית, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates), while the consequent's verb, masculine or feminine, agrees with its own subject ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים חדשים תשלם הרשות, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), and a plural future verb ends in ו as no adjective does.
- Within a condition what follows a verb-shaped word tells the consequent's verb: a plural one ends in ו and a singular one is followed by its definite subject ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים לעובד ישלם המעסיק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), which no adjective or construct complement is ("אחוזים מדמי אבטלה, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates); and a lexical ש-word such as "שכיר" opens no relative clause.
- Within a condition the consequent's verb is known by word, a closed list of the third-person future forms a statute writes its consequents in plus the plural that begins in י and ends in ו, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים לעובד ישלם מעסיק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500 while "אחוזים מהכנסת יחיד החייב במס, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates; and ש fused to a preposition with its suffix ("שעליה", "שבגינה") opens a relative clause.
- Within a condition the consequent's verb is known by word alone, a closed lexicon of the third-person future forms a statute writes its consequents in, singular and plural ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים יקבל העובד, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), so no spelling counts as a verb and the possessive "יבולו" modifies its noun ("אחוזים מערך יבולו, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates); and ש with a suffixed "ממנה" opens a relative clause.
- Within a condition a word after a construct-state noun is its complement whatever the verb lexicon says of its spelling ("אחוזים מהכנסת תושב ישראל, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates), the noun homographs (תושב, תורה, תעלה, יוסף, תוסף) leave the lexicon, and ש before a construct subject with its definite complement ("שפקיד השומה יקבע") opens a relative clause.
- Within a condition no ending marks a construct head, so a verb after a feminine noun still splits the list ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים לעובדת ישלם המעסיק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), and a relative clause on any subject, definite or not, shows itself by its own verb ("אחוזים מההכנסה שבית דין יקבע, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates).
- Within a condition a ש-word the verb follows at once is a one-word subject and no relative prefix ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שותפה תשלם, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), while a relative subject of two words or more shows its own verb within six words ("אחוזים מההכנסה שבית דין אזורי לעבודה יקבע, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates).
- Within a condition ש before ו is a root letter, never the relative prefix, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שוכרת הדירה תשלם, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500, while the relative ש on any subject, one word or titled, shows its verb within six words ("אחוזים מההכנסה ששופט יקבע, תחול ההוראה" reads three rates); the ועדה family is the exception.
- Within a condition the doubled-vav spelling "שוועדת" joins the ועדה exception to the root-letter rule, and the lexical ש-nouns a statute uses (שליח, שכן, שמאי) are listed, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שליח החברה ישלם, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500. (, )
- A listed ש-noun in any inflection hides no verb ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שליחים ישלמו, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500); a bare ש-word outside the list is undecided, its verb decides nothing, and the list is reported ambiguous ("מההכנסה ששופט יקבע,"); the ועדה family is a relative marker in either spelling; and "שתים" and "מאתים" read as two and two hundred.
- A possessive on a ש-root ("שוכריו ישלמו", "שולחיו ישלמו") is no relative marker, ש before ו being a root letter, so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שוכריו ישלמו, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500; and the traditional tens "שלשים", "חמשים" and "ששים" read as thirty, fifty and sixty.
- A suffix moves a listed ש-noun's final letter to its medial form, so "שכנו ישלם" and "שחקניו ישלמו" hide no verb ("אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שכנו ישלם, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500), while the unmistakable relative markers ("שממנו", "שעליה", the ועדה family) are read before the lexical nouns; and the traditional units "חמשה" and "שלש" read as five and three, alone, in teens, in percentages and before a scale word.
- A ש-word that is both a relative marker and a listed noun ("שמו", his name or that from him) decides nothing and the list is reported ambiguous; only base stems inflect, so "שממנו" stays the preposition it is; and the ambiguity report reads each member as the source does, sign and fraction included ("10, -עשרים" grounds as 10, -20; "1⁄2" as 0.5).
- A listed ש-noun inflects from its base ("שם" gives "שמנו", both marker and noun, so the list is reported ambiguous) while an entry that is itself an inflection stays fixed ("שממנו" remains the preposition); fraction words and glyphs are list body and endpoints ("השיעורים הם שני שלישים, 10 ו־30 אחוזים" shares the unit; "½" is a printed endpoint); a mixed ASCII fraction in Hebrew text is one number ("2 1/2" is 2.5); and an English percent word after a fraction slash scales it ("10 1⁄4 percent" is 0.1025).
- A feminine listed ש-noun takes its possessives on the ת construct stem ("שליחתו", "שאלתו"), so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שליחתו תקבל את המענק, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500; a vulgar-fraction glyph is read in every list position, the unit-bearing last member ("10, 20 ו־½ אחוז") and after a soft wrap included; and in Hebrew text a bare ASCII fraction ("1/2") and a whole with a glyph ("2½") are one number, so the ambiguity report claims only what extraction grounds.
- A listed ש-noun takes its possessives on the plural stem too ("שאלותיו", "שליחותיו"), so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שאלותיו יועברו לוועדה, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500; a vulgar-fraction glyph, bare or after a whole, signed or not, is one number that a percent marker after it makes a rate ("10, 20 ו־2½%" is three rates) and that a scaled amount's remainder includes ("3 אלפים ו־2½ שקלים" is 3,002.5).
- A listed ש-noun takes its second-person possessives too ("שאלתך", "שאלתכם"), so "אם התשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים שאלתך תועבר לוועדה, והיתרה תוחזר" keeps 500; a bare glyph is a scaled amount's remainder ("3 אלפים ו־½ שקלים" is 3,000.5); a glyph rate keeps its fractional tail ("2½% וחצי" is 0.03); and a thousands-grouped whole joins its glyph ("1,000½" is 1,000.5).
- A negative glyph rate applies its sign after its fractional tail ("-2½% וחצי" is -0.03), a fraction-slash rate keeps its fractional tail ("2 1⁄2% וחצי" is 0.03), and a thousands-grouped whole joins a slash fraction ("1,000 1/2" and "1,000 1⁄2" are 1,000.5).
- A fractional tail after a percent marker joins the rate with a maqaf on its conjunction too ("2½% ו־חצי" is 0.03, "2½% ו־שלושה רבעים" is 0.0325), so the tail is consumed wherever it is suppressed.
- Every fractional tail on a conjunction joins its number with a maqaf too ("2.5 אחוז ו־חצי" is 0.03, "3 מיליון ו־חצי" is 3,500,000), so a tail is consumed wherever it is suppressed.
- A maqaf or hyphen after a one-letter prefix binds it to its word, so "3 ו־חצי אחוזים" is 0.035 and "שלושה ו־חצי מיליון שקלים" is 3,500,000, as their plain "וחצי" forms are.
- A prefix's separator is stripped whether it is a maqaf or an ASCII hyphen, in the number-prefix reader and in the compound parser's word reader, so "ב-מיליון וחצי" is 1,500,000, "כ-עשרים ושלושה" is 23 and "עשרים ו־שלושה אחוזים" is 0.23.
- Every reader that drops a maqaf after a prefix drops an ASCII hyphen too, so the definite ordinal "ה-שני" is the ordinal it is ("הילד ה-שני אחוז וחצי" keeps 2 and reads 0.015) and a hyphen-bound range endpoint joins its range ("משניים ל-שלושה אחוזים" is 0.02 to 0.03, "בין שלושה ל-חמישה מיליון" three to five million).
- Every Hebrew prefix pattern takes its separator the same way: a prefix or the article binds to its word directly, across a maqaf or across an ASCII hyphen, in the number readers, the structural references and their lists, the list headings, the measured-second guard, the money contexts, the conditional markers and the relative markers alike ("ל־חצי שנייה" is half a second and no ordinal; "התוספת ה-שנייה" is a schedule, not a two; "ה־שיעורים הם 10, 20 ו־30 אחוזים" heads its list).
- An ASCII hyphen after a one-letter Hebrew prefix is the maqaf it stands for: the numeric text view rewrites it in place before any pattern runs, so every reader sees "ו־מאתיים", "מ־הכנסה", "ה־תקציב" and "ו־חצי" whether the source set a maqaf or a hyphen, and the two spellings ground, recall and extract the same values everywhere.
- A maqaf after a Hebrew prefix before a word binds the prefix as attachment does: the numeric text view moves the prefix cluster up to its word in place, so "ו־עד", "ו־המתינה" and "ה־שיעורים" are "ועד", "והמתינה" and "השיעורים" to every reader, and the attached, maqaf and hyphen spellings ground, recall and extract the same values everywhere.
- The prefix stack the numeric text view binds across a maqaf or a hyphen is the grammar's own: the conjunction, then ש or כש, then a preposition or the article ("וכש־המתינה", "כשה־שיעורים", "ומה־שכר"), so every stack reads as its attached form; a plural heading noun carries the same stack, and a "כש" in it opens the condition ("כשהתשלומים הם 500, 2 או 3 מיליון שקלים ישולמו" splits at the consequent as "כאשר התשלומים" does).
- A condition whose relative ש binds the heading noun ("ככל שהתשלומים הם", "במקרה שהשיעורים הם") opens the condition as "כאשר" before the noun does, so the list splits at a consequent verb and closes at a tail under every marker and every spelling of the prefix.
- The spelled zero "אפס" is a Hebrew numeral: a list of rates that starts at zero ("השיעורים הם אפס, 10 ו־20 אחוזים") shares its unit across every member as the printed "0, 10 ו־20" does, and a zero floor, rate or range endpoint reads as the printed zero reads.
- A list that shares a unit is read to its grammatical boundary however many members it has: the backward walks that carry a percent noun or a printed scale across "10, 11, …, 27 ו־28 אחוזים" no longer stop after a fixed number of steps, the walk back to a list's heading runs to the sentence stop rather than 160 characters, and a colon-terminated currency heading governs to the end of its paragraph rather than 240 characters, so the first members of a long list keep the unit the last one names.
- A list of any length is read in time proportional to its length: the walk that carries a shared unit back over a list learns the list's heading once instead of once per member, the paragraph and currency-heading scopes are indexed once per text, trailing whitespace is trimmed in place rather than by copying the prefix, and the forward scan to a list's end runs to the list's boundary rather than 240 characters, so a conditional list of seventy rates keeps its unit and a text of thousands of clauses or members costs no more than its size.
- A list wrapped onto an indented line keeps its shared unit ("10,\n            20 ו־30 אחוזים"): a bounded backward search measures its window before the whitespace that ends at its position, and a blank line in that whitespace stays a boundary; and a list inside a condition is decided by the boundary that decides it however long the clause between ("אחוזים מההכנסה החייבת אשר שולמה … הבקשה, תחול ההוראה" closes it), never by a count of words.
- The last fixed windows in the Hebrew grammar give way to the clause: padding before a line wrap no longer hides the comma that joins a list, a rate word reaches its pair across any modifiers in its clause ("הריבית השנתית החלה על יתרת ההלוואה הכוללת תהיה 10 או 30%" is two rates), and a money context reaches its amount across any of its connectors.
- A rate word reaches the pair it governs and no further: across the modifiers of its own expression, never across a new predicate ("יוטל") or an amount noun that governs the pair itself ("קנס של 50 או 2%" is fifty shekels and two percent), and across a line wrap but not a blank line; a money noun reaches its amount across any spacing or wrap in its sentence ("הקנס … יהיה 3 מיליון ו־30 ימי מאסר" is a fine and a term).
- A rate's predicate keeps its own connectors ("הריבית תעמוד על 10 או 30%", "תהיה לפחות", "תהיה בשיעור של" are two rates), and a reference number between the rate word and a separate fine ("לפי סעיף 5") no longer hides the fine's own noun from the check that keeps the rate away from it.
- A rate word's reach is read as a phrase: its subject with attributives, relative clauses and prepositional phrases ("הריבית על ההלוואה", "הריבית השנתית החלה על יתרת ההלוואה הכוללת"), its predicate whether a future verb, a copula, a participle or a bare predicative ("תהיה", "היא", "עומדת", "גבוהה"), and the predicate's connectors ("על", "לפחות", "בשיעור של"); a new subject ("אז הקנס יהיה 50 או 2%") or a second predicate takes the pair away.
- A rate word's subject phrase keeps its relative clauses and construct complements ("הריבית שהבנק גובה היא 10 או 30%", "הריבית על הלוואת עובד תהיה 10 או 30%" are two rates), a definite amount noun that no phrase holds is the subject of the predicate after it ("אז הקנס יהיה 50 או 2%" is fifty shekels), and every rate word in a clause is a candidate, so a later "בשיעור של" governs its pair when an earlier rate's expression has ended.
- A relative clause in a rate's subject keeps its own predicate ("הריבית שהבנק יקבע תהיה 10 או 30%", "הריבית אשר הבנק יקבע תהיה" are two rates), and a consequent's subject keeps its attributives before its predicate ("הקנס המרבי יהיה 50 או 2%" is fifty shekels).
- A rate's main predicate is the last one before its pair, so every relative clause in the subject keeps its own verb whatever opened it ("הריבית שבנק ישראל יקבע תהיה 10 או 30%" is two rates), and a consequent's subject is found by walking back over all its modifiers ("הקנס הקבוע בחוק יהיה 50 או 2%" is fifty shekels).
- The subject a predicate is predicated of is the last noun phrase no earlier phrase holds, its modifiers of any length held with it ("הקנס לפי הוראת בנק ישראל יהיה 50 או 2%", "הקנס שבנק ישראל יקבע יהיה", "קנס הפיגורים יהיה" are fifty shekels each), so a rate word reaches only a pair whose subject is its own.
- An amount noun is read by its own letters before any prefix is seen in them ("מענק הפיצוי יהיה 50 או 2%", "שכר העובד יהיה" are fifty shekels, not "from" or "that" anything), and a preposition attached to its object keeps the object's article ("גבוהה מהמותר הקנס יהיה" reads as "מן המותר" does).
- An amount noun is known in its plural and suffixed forms ("התשלומים יהיו 50 או 2%", "תשלומיו יהיו" are fifty shekels), and a clause adverb closes the phrase before it ("מהמותר בחוק אז הקנס יהיה" reads as "מן המותר אז הקנס יהיה" does).
- A fraction of a plural or suffixed amount noun is the fraction ("חמישית מתשלומי העובד" is a fifth of the payments, 0.2, not a fifth grade), since every pattern built from the amount-noun stems now knows the forms a suffix gives them.
- A fraction's base is an amount noun in one of its inflections and no other word: "דרגה חמישית המסומנת בטבלה" is a fifth grade, since "המסומנת" names no tax, while "חמישית מהמסים" is a fifth of the taxes.
- An amount noun is known in the inflections a noun takes and no others: a feminine or plural ending, then a possessive ("מסו", "מסיו", "הכנסתו", "קצבאות"), with the possessive never after the article, so "חמישית ממסו" is a fifth of the tax and "בבדיקה חמישית הערכנו" stays a fifth check.
- A feminine amount noun is known in its plural and possessed plural ("משכורותיו", "עלויות", "ריביות"), the tax noun in every possessive ("מסם"), and an ordinal after the noun it agrees with stays an ordinal before a definite noun that begins the next phrase ("בדרגה חמישית השכר גבוה יותר" is a fifth grade; "חמישית השכר" is a fifth of the wage).
- An ordinal after any feminine noun stays an ordinal before a definite noun that begins the next phrase ("בבדיקה חמישית השכר נמצא תקין", "בעיר חמישית השכר גבוה" are a fifth inspection and a fifth city), a balance and a benefit are amount nouns ("חמישית מיתרת החשבון", "חמישית מההטבות" are fifths), and a supplement of a fraction of an amount ("תוספת חמישית מהשכר") is an amount to encode, not a schedule reference.
- A verb or copula before a fraction word is clause context whatever letter it ends in ("המעסיקה שילמה חמישית השכר", "הקצבה הייתה חמישית השכר" are fifths of the wage), and a supplement of a fraction under any explicit partitive ("תוספת חמישית מן השכר", "מתוך השכר", "של השכר") is an amount to encode, not a schedule reference.
- A predicate before a fraction word is clause context under a conjunction or relative prefix too ("חישבה ושילמה חמישית השכר", "הקצבה שהייתה חמישית השכר" are fifths of the wage); "מן" after an ordinal is a noun modifier when it names a kind ("בדיקה חמישית מן הסוג הזה" is a fifth test) and a partitive otherwise; and a supplement of a fraction of anything but the statute itself ("תוספת חמישית מן התקבולים", "מן השטח") is an amount to encode.
- A schedule reference stays a reference before a verb or the statute's construct form ("התוספת השנייה מגדירה תשלום", "של פקודת מס הכנסה"), since only a fraction-shaped ordinal before a partitive is a fraction; the future "תהווה" is a predicate like "מהווה"; and "מן" after an ordinal a feminine noun carries is a whole's partitive only where it names an amount ("פנייה חמישית מן הציבור" is a fifth request).
- A schedule reference is unmasked only where the fraction reader itself reads a fraction ("התוספת החמישית מהווה חלק מהחוק" stays the fifth schedule), and a verb of paying, including or constituting anywhere earlier in the clause says a fraction follows, a recipient between them or not ("שילם לעובדת החדשה חמישית השכר", "הקצבה כוללת חמישית מן התקבולים" are fifths).
- A verb earlier in the clause governs a fraction word across a prepositional phrase and no further ("שילם לעובדת החדשה חמישית השכר" is a fifth; "קיבל פנייה חמישית מן הציבור" is a fifth request), and a schedule's statute is named in its construct form too ("תוספת חמישית של פקודת מס הכנסה" is a schedule).
- A verb of paying governs a fraction word across its recipient and no further: a phrase in ל with whatever modifies the recipient ("שילם לעובדת חדשה חמישית השכר", "לעובדת בשם דנה" are fifths of the wage), while a bare noun after the verb ("קיבל בקשה חמישית") keeps its ordinal; and a schedule's statute is named in every construct form ("של הוראת השעה", "של החלטת הממשלה").
- Only a verb of paying governs a fraction word across its recipient, and only a fraction of an amount: the recipient keeps its name and its possessor ("לעובדת בשם שירה", "לעובדת של החברה" are paid a fifth of the wage), a receiving verb's object keeps its ordinal ("קיבלה לוחית חמישית" is a fifth plate), and a recipient's own ordinal stays ("שילם לעובדת חמישית מן העובדות הזכאיות" pays a fifth employee).
- The verbs that pay an amount are one vocabulary wherever the reader asks about them ("נתן לעובדת חמישית השכר", "הקצה", "מנכה" pay a fifth of the wage), and receipts, redemptions, royalties, advances, deposits and refunds are amount nouns ("חמישית מן התקבולים" is a fifth of the receipts).
- A fraction's count takes the traditional spellings ("שלש עשיריות האחוז" is 0.003, "חמשה רבעים" 1.25), a fraction takes a bare construct or possessed amount as its operand in a paying clause ("ישלם לעובד חמישית שכרו", "חמישית שכר המינימום"), the paying vocabulary knows the past, present and passive forms ("ניתנה", "הפקיד", "העניק", "משולם"), and a bonus is an amount.
- A fraction's operand is read by the partitive the pattern consumed, not by a noun's first letter ("בדרגה חמישית משכורתו" stays a fifth grade); a count takes the construct "שלשת" and is whatever number the numeral grammar reads before the fraction word ("עשר עשיריות האחוז" is 0.01, "אחת עשרה עשיריות" 0.011, "מאה עשיריות" 10), a vav-bound last word leaving the fraction word a mixed number's tail ("עשרים ושלוש עשיריות" stays 20.3); a blank line separates a count from a fraction word.
- The count the numeral grammar reads counts a construct-form fraction too ("עשרים רבעי השכר" is 5) and may carry a scale word ("אלף שמיניות האחוז" is 1.25); a partitive between a fractional count and the percent noun binds them ("שלוש עשיריות של האחוז" is 0.003); a fraction word's operand, partitive and unit follow it across wrap space only, so a blank line or a paragraph separator leaves "דרגה חמישית" a fifth grade.
- A printed number flush before a plural or construct fraction word is its count ("3 עשיריות האחוז" is 0.003, "ל־3 רבעי השכר" 0.75); a spelled count is set aside only where the numeral grammar reads it and the fraction word as one mixed number, so "מאה ועשרים עשיריות האחוז" is 0.12 while "עשרים ושלוש עשיריות" stays 20.3; a number before a singular fraction word is no count; the percent sign after a spelled number binds across wrap space only, so "דרגה חמישית" before a blank line and "%" stays a fifth grade.
- The counted-fraction vocabulary carries every plural the fraction table does ("שלוש רביעיות" is 0.75, "שתי שלישיות" two thirds); a printed whole with a spelled tail counts a fraction word ("3 וחצי עשיריות האחוז" is 0.0035, "ל־3 וחצי עשיריות מהשכר" 0.35) and is not read again on its own; the percent sign after a printed figure binds across wrap space only, so "3 וחצי" before a blank line and "%" is three and a half.
- A printed count with a vulgar-fraction glyph or a slash fraction ("3½ עשיריות", "3 1/2 עשיריות", "3 1⁄2 עשיריות") counts the fraction word after it: the glyph, ASCII-mixed and slash-fraction passes yield the figure to the fraction reader, so "ל־3½ עשיריות מהשכר" is 0.35 and "3½ עשיריות האחוז" 0.0035.
- A printed count with a fraction word is a range endpoint: "בין 2 עשיריות ל־3 עשיריות האחוז" runs from 0.002 to 0.003 (with a printed mixed count too, "2 וחצי עשיריות" 0.0025), as the spelled "בין שתי עשיריות לשלוש עשיריות האחוז" did.
- A scale word inside a counted fraction's count is the count's alone ("בין 500 עשיריות לאלף עשיריות האחוז" runs from 0.5 to 1), a counted fraction endpoint is complete on its own, and a bare endpoint before a counted fraction shares its fraction word ("בין שתיים לשלוש עשיריות האחוז" runs from 0.002).
- A range endpoint is classified before a bare endpoint shares the fraction word of the counted fraction after it: a fraction of its own ("בין חצי לשלושה רבעים האחוז" runs from 0.005) shares nothing, a mixed number's tail ("בין 2 ל־3 ושלושה רבעים אחוזים" runs from 0.02) is no unit, a partitive after the counted fraction ("שלוש עשיריות של האחוז") hides no unit, and a mixed count of a fraction word ("2 וחצי עשיריות") is complete.
- A printed fraction ("½", "1/2", "1⁄2") and a signed fraction word ("−חצי") are fractions of their own at a range endpoint, so "בין ½ לשלושה רבעים האחוז" runs from 0.005; a signed bare number and a printed mixed number ("2½") still take the counted fraction's word.
- A fraction of its own before the percent noun is a rate whatever the order ("בין ½ ל־3 עשיריות האחוז" and "בין חצי לבין שלוש עשיריות האחוז" run from 0.005), while the ascending guard on a "בין" range of bare numbers now holds for an attached connector too ("בין 500 לשלושה אחוזים" is no range of rates).
- Where a rate word governs the clause, a "בין" range shares its percent noun whatever the order of a number a rate could be ("שיעור המס יהיה בין 5 ל־3 אחוזים" runs from 0.05, and "בין 3½ ל־2½ אחוזים" from 0.035); a number no rate could be ("בין 500 ל־3 אחוזים") and a pair with no rate word keep the ascending guard.
- A rate word governing the clause makes a descending "בין" pair a range of rates whatever the size of the endpoints ("שיעור הזיכוי יהיה בין 100 ל־90 אחוזים" runs from 1, "בין 150 ל־125 אחוזים" from 1.5), and the reviewed "השיעור הוא בין 500 ל־3 אחוזים" reads the same way; with no rate word the ascending guard keeps a bare number off the noun.
- "בין … ובין …" joins a bounded range as "בין … לבין …" does ("שיעור המס יהיה בין 2 ובין 3 אחוזים" runs from 0.02), and a printed number may begin at its decimal point in every Hebrew reader and in the direct percentage reader (".5 אחוזים" and ".5%" are 0.005, ".5% וחצי" 0.01, "בין .5 ל־3 אחוזים" runs from 0.005).
- "בין … ובין …" joins a shared-scale range as "לבין" does ("הסכום יהיה בין 5 ובין 7 מיליון שקלים" runs from five million, "בין 5 ובין 7 אלפים אחוזים" from 50), across a line wrap after the join too; and the cleaner detaches a maqaf before a decimal point that digits follow, so "הקצבה תוכפל ב־.5" reads 0.5 with its source span.
- A shared-scale range of rates under a rate word shares its scale whatever its order ("שיעור המס יהיה בין 7 ובין 5 אלפים אחוזים" runs from 70), a range of amounts still ascending; the direct percentage reader takes the Unicode minus ("−.5%" is −0.005, the span keeping the sign); and a bidirectional mark or a currency sign detaches before a leading decimal ("₪.5" is 0.5) as before a digit.
- A bidirectional mark inside a numeric token is nothing to the cleaner and the direct percentage reader ("−‏.5%" and "−.5‏%" are −0.005); a fraction before a scaled upper endpoint, counted or not, takes the scale through the shared-scale pass ("בין חצי לבין 3 אלפים אחוזים" runs from 5); and a comma-grouped number with a decimal part is read whole ("1,234.5%" is 12.345), a comma-grouped whole in Hebrew text being grouped thousands.
- A bidirectional mark inside a numeric token is dropped before any other mark is spaced, and after a fraction glyph as after a digit ("−‏.5 אחוזים" is −0.005, "½‏%" 0.005); a comma-grouped whole with more than one group is grouped thousands in any script ("1,234,567%" is 12,345.67).
